Licence
=======

This repository contains three kinds of material and they are covered separately.

1. Our own work
---------------

The manifests, the tag register, the glossaries, the corpus structure, the reports and the translations are copyright (c) 2026 tamnd and are released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence.

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

2. The metadata
---------------

The bibliographic metadata under metadata/ describes every paper on arXiv and is derived from arXiv's own metadata, which arXiv publishes into the public domain under CC0 1.0.

    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

That is why the metadata plane covers all of arXiv while the content plane covers a small fraction of it. Metadata needs no licence gate. Content does.

3. The papers
-------------

The text, mathematics, tables and figures extracted from each paper remain under the licence that paper's author chose on submission, which is recorded per paper and per version in the paper's own front matter together with the source URL and the SHA-256 of the file it was read from.

arXiv offers a submitter six licences and we sort them into four access classes.

    cc0, cc-by                      open         extract, translate, publish
    cc-by-sa, cc-by-nc-sa           share-alike  the same, and our files carry the same licence
    cc-by-nc-nd                     verbatim     extract and publish, no translation
    arxiv-1.0                       record       metadata and a linked abstract only

A translation is a derivative work, so a no-derivatives licence forbids one. arXiv's default licence is a nonexclusive distribution licence that grants arXiv the right to distribute and grants nobody else the right to republish, so a paper under it gets a bibliographic record and a link and nothing else.

Nothing is extracted unless the recorded licence says it may be. A paper with no licence recorded is treated as though it were under the default, which is the strictest of the six, and gets nothing.

Figures are reproduced only for papers in the open and share-alike classes, at the resolution the source carries and no higher.

The provenance record
---------------------

Every extracted paper carries the arXiv id, the version, the licence of that version, the extraction path, the source URL and the checksum. A licence is a property of a version and not of a paper, so a v1 under CC BY and a v2 under the default licence are two different decisions and the record keeps them apart.

If you are an author and you want your paper removed from this corpus, open an issue and it will be removed, whatever the recorded licence says.
